00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:59.703
&gt;&gt; Now, I understand that when
you took the government's shares,

00:12:59.703 --> 00:13:03.597
what you inherited was a bank
with far too many employees,

00:13:03.597 --> 00:13:08.866
a high portfolio of non-performing loans,
and it was not very well managed.

00:13:08.866 --> 00:13:10.833
That's a dumb-
&gt;&gt; And highly politicized.

00:13:10.833 --> 00:13:15.769
&gt;&gt; So what business does a guy who never
ran a bank have jumping into that?

00:13:15.769 --> 00:13:17.993
&gt;&gt; Interesting that you
asked that question.

00:13:17.993 --> 00:13:22.652
There's a Japanese saying that
sometimes you have to jump through

00:13:22.652 --> 00:13:25.403
a window not knowing what's outside.

00:13:25.403 --> 00:13:32.048
And the knowledge of exactly what
the problems are is itself a constraint.

00:13:32.048 --> 00:13:36.887
And therefore, I think that if I
had known too much about banking,

00:13:36.887 --> 00:13:41.395
I may not have done it,
I may have said, this is just too much.

00:13:41.395 --> 00:13:47.586
But in that sense, I wasn't professional
banker, I was just an MBA who just

00:13:47.586 --> 00:13:54.001
had a certain overconfidence that MBAs
have that any problem can be analyzed.

00:13:54.001 --> 00:13:57.285
Can be assessed as
a problem of management,

00:13:57.285 --> 00:14:02.269
a strategy can emanate from it,
and you should be able to execute.

00:14:02.269 --> 00:14:05.702
And that was my going in
approach to the matter.

00:14:05.702 --> 00:14:09.524
&gt;&gt; Hakeem's story isn't just
about the problems he faced,

00:14:09.524 --> 00:14:11.632
it's about how he solved them.

00:14:11.632 --> 00:14:15.860
&gt;&gt; You've got to start shifting
who are the customer base.

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:18.914
How are the procedures improved upon.

00:14:18.914 --> 00:14:24.282
How do people get into the culture
of marketing when they've really

00:14:24.282 --> 00:14:29.193
been accustomed to people coming
in to see them as the banker.

00:14:29.193 --> 00:14:33.591
They don't see the banking as
a service industry in a sense,

00:14:33.591 --> 00:14:39.124
a lot of it has to do with the prestige
of people coming to you to borrow money.

00:14:39.124 --> 00:14:40.445
&gt;&gt; So I love this point.

00:14:40.445 --> 00:14:47.114
So, I want you to share with me a moment,
a critical inflection point,

00:14:47.114 --> 00:14:51.227
where you needed the bank's leadership and

00:14:51.227 --> 00:14:57.695
staff to adopt your cultural mindset
about what this bank should be.

00:14:57.695 --> 00:15:00.477
Is this a matter of very
slow incremental change?

00:15:00.477 --> 00:15:02.739
Was there an all hands meeting in-
&gt;&gt; No.

00:15:02.739 --> 00:15:06.446
&gt;&gt; The conference hall where you said,
folks, this is who we are going to be?

00:15:06.446 --> 00:15:08.985
&gt;&gt; No, I think there was never one,
there was several.

00:15:08.985 --> 00:15:13.474
But the one that always hits me
the most is the time at which I kind

00:15:13.474 --> 00:15:17.625
of laid out our situation,
our financial situation, and

00:15:17.625 --> 00:15:21.544
why we're going to have to
do certain kinds of things.

00:15:21.544 --> 00:15:25.340
I did it on a Thursday or Friday,
and on Monday the workers and

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:30.414
some of the management had taken over the
